TTP_ALLOWED_HOSTS at `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:359`, but line 359 is the mcp service's `dockerfile:` line; the actual allowlist value (`${REBAR_MCP_HTTP_ALLOWED_HOSTS:-rebar.solutions.navateam.com}`) lives at line 395. The value, file, and the select_probe_host case-(1) reasoning built on it are all correct — only the line number is wrong.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fea8648085fedbd5a","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / 'Probe Host' paragraph: 'rebar.solutions.navateam.com (infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:359)'","norm_id":"nf9582a91eab24d24","priority":0.44,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader following the citation to confirm the box's probe-host source lands on the build stanza, not the env value."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Change '(infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:359)' to '(infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:395)'.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify the hand-rolled in-lifespan scope/receive/send drive against the established in-process ASGI harnesses (asgi-lifespan LifespanManager, Starlette TestClient, httpx.ASGITransport, or the SDK's session_manager.run() lifespan wiring): state why the lifespan-ordering requirement is not met by, or is better served than, those alternatives.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6057,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'Drive one real initialize through this server's own StreamableHTTPSessionManager inside the ASGI lifespan … The probe calls mcp.session_manager.handle_request(scope, receive, send)'","Retrieved source (starlette.io/lifespan) confirms the ordering premise, and (asgi-lifespan PyPI) documents a LifespanManager that programmatically sends lifespan events + drives requests without a server — the established shape for exactly this","Retrieved MCP SDK issue #713 shows the SDK's own supported pattern is passing session_manager.run() into the app lifespan; the plan wraps app.router.lifespan_context instead and never contrasts the two","The plan does affirmatively consider prior art for the GATE half (store gate mobile-groovy-badger, DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS) but is silent on alternatives for the handshake-drive half"],"finding":"The novel pattern — hand-rolling a raw ASGI scope/receive/send drive of the server's own StreamableHTTPSessionManager embedded inside the lifespan — is committed to without weighing the established in-process request-driving harnesses (asgi-lifespan's LifespanManager, Starlette TestClient, httpx.ASGITransport, or the SDK's own session_manager.run() lifespan wiring) that solve 'drive a real request through this app in-process'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1bdba90b90152397","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section ('Drive one real initialize through this server's own StreamableHTTPSessionManager inside the ASGI lifespan'); Conclusive paragraph ('The probe calls mcp.session_manager.handle_request(scope, receive, send)')","norm_id":"n4aee4d9b471e00e9","priority":0.0943,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or future maintainer asks why a raw scope/receive/send drive was hand-built rather than reusing a tested ASGI harness, and the plan has no recorded answer","The hand-rolled scope dict omits or mis-shapes a field the transport expects, a class of bug the established harnesses avoid by construction"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a short 'considered alternatives' note to the Approach: e.g. 'A TestClient/httpx.ASGITransport probe cannot run *before* lifespan.startup.complete because those harnesses drive the fully-assembled app; only wrapping app.router.lifespan_context lets the handshake complete inside the startup context, which is the ordering the whole implication rests on' — or, if a harness can be used, prefer it over hand-constructing the scope.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"28f0b0fc9c60244f","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["3e89cfacf